@*
    One layout for every page. All styling lives in site.css and all behaviour in
    site.js — nothing inline anywhere — because the Content-Security-Policy in
    ServiceDefaults carries no 'unsafe-inline'. An inline <style> or onclick added here
    will fail visibly in the browser console rather than quietly requiring the policy to
    be weakened.
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>@ViewData["Title"]</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Group texts, easier. Paste a roster, get a link that opens a group message with everyone already in it." />
    <link rel="icon" href="~/favicon.ico" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/site.css" asp-append-version="true" />

    @* In <head>, and render-blocking on purpose. It applies a saved dark choice to <html>
       before the first paint; loaded at the bottom with site.js it would instead produce a
       flash of the light palette on every navigation. It is a file rather than an inline
       script because script-src carries no 'unsafe-inline'. *@
    <script src="~/js/theme.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
</head>
<body>
    @*
        The wordmark is type, not an image. It was an SVG whose viewBox was the invalid
        string "0 0" — with no intrinsic aspect ratio the browser fell back to a 300px box
        and the glyphs floated inside it, which is what made the logo look clipped and
        indented. Setting it as real type fixes it and removes the asset.

        .bar is an inner wrapper so the rule under the header spans the window while its
        contents line up with the page below.
    *@
    <header class="site-header">
        <div class="bar">
            <a class="brand" href="/">SMSer<span class="brand-dot">.</span></a>
            <span class="bar-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <p class="tagline">Making group text management a little easier</p>

            @* Ships hidden and is revealed by theme.js, like the photo control: without
               JavaScript it could not switch anything, and the page is light regardless. *@
            <button type="button" class="theme-toggle" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" hidden>Dark</button>

            <a class="bar-source" href="https://github.com/nhudacin/smser" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source</a>
        </div>
    </header>

    <main class="site-main">
        @RenderBody()
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
        <div class="bar">
            <span class="brand">SMSer<span class="brand-dot">.</span></span>
            <span class="bar-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span>By Nick Hudacin</span>
            <a class="bar-source" href="https://github.com/nhudacin/smser" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source</a>
        </div>
    </footer>

    <script src="~/js/site.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
    @await RenderSectionAsync("Scripts", required: false)
</body>
</html>
